{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558280-mage-build-guys-i-m-a-fox","id":1558280,"title":"Mage build, ''Guys I'm a Fox''","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-02-13T04:46:58-08:00","id":1558280,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Mage build, ''Guys I'm a Fox''","content":"Hey folks,<br /> <br /> I\u2019m building a very newly Awakened character (like\u2026A day or two in lol) and I\u2019m looking for advice on the spheres.<br /> <br /> The concept: He genuinely believes he\u2019s a kitsune or some mythical fox creature. Whether that\u2019s a delusion, an Avatar expressing itself through myth, or something stranger is intentionally unclear. Awakening, to him, felt less like discovering magic and more like <i>''Oh yeah, I remember what I am'' </i><br /> <br /> Because of that worldview, he\u2019ll almost certainly gravitate toward the <b>Disparate Alliance</b>. He doesn\u2019t think of himself as a mage at all his \u201cmagic\u201d is just innate abilities expressed through folklore, instincts, and small rituals rather than formal spell casting.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, we\u2019re starting <i>very</i> light:<br /> - \u2019ll only have <b>access to two Spheres total</b>. One Sphere at <b>level 2</b> and one Sphere at <b>level 1</b>, and <b>Arete 2</b>. But I\u2019ll be able to improve them in play<br /> <br /> I have thought on Correspondence with Mind, Forces or Spirit. tho I cannot decide. Which would be your advice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28959-damedrac","name":"Damedrac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-13T05:55:29-08:00","id":1558281,"title":"","content":"Kitsune are archetypal tricksters. Forces 2 would be good to disguise yourself trough illusions. Mind 1 it's overal great, and also could be important to understand emotions and manipulate them. Spirit 1 could be good if your character it's friends with spirits (trough backgrounds). <hr />And I know you didn't ask, but I don't see how the concept gravitates towards the Disparate, save, maybe, for the Hollow Ones (that would just accept whatever as long as he's &quot;romantic&quot; somehow). Disparate tend to be more rigid with their cultural background and practices than the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Closest non-Marauder that come to mind:<br /> <br /> The Verbena often believe their magick comes from magical bloodlines. I could see some Verbena-like families believing their ancestor was a fox. So you have reasons to believe you could be a fox.<br /> <br /> Some weird dreamspeakers that were taught by spirits also come to mind - such a character could have been led to believe his soul it's that of a kitsune (something interesting about this is that, if his Avatar manifest that way, the mage's own spiritual body could resemble a kitsune while in the Umbra).<br /> <br /> Of course, you could be an Orphan and just ally with whomever. <hr /> It isn't normal for Mages to just get a random &quot;delusion&quot; imposed on them when they Awaken (unless they awake to Marauderdoom). They, if anything, see reality more clearly than ever - then delude themselves because everyone has to understand what they see under some parameter or pre-conception, and a mage's power adjusts to better fit those parametters.<br /> <br /> A mage could believe he's a Kitsune because his Avatar it's one and they saw themselves reflected as such on Dreams. Or because of ancient legends on his locale talking about fox-people living among humans that have the powers you manifested at a time of peril - &quot;you're a fox, Harry&quot;. Maybe they were a therian that already believed to be a fox, so now that he's magick I guess he has to be a <i>magical</i> fox ... etc ... If I were the ST, I would ask why you suddenly became to believe you're a fox. Unless the character it's being manipulated by some entity that wants them to believe that uncritically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 02-13-2026, 09:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T04:10:39-08:00","id":1558314,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get a hold of the old Werewolf Players guide I think they had Ware-Foxes in them and I think they had a Bread Book and showed up in the Year of the East books<br /> <br /> Perhaps you are a kitsune Kinfolk and instead of going through the Change you Awakened get a &quot;Warewolf Companion&quot; only 3 Freebie Points or if you don't want a connection to the actual kitsune take a few levels in Past Lives and Throwback to a past life that was a kitsune and take some magical prohibitions that line up with the kitsune. or mix and match from all of the above.<br /> <br /> try to model your Rotes after the kitsune Bread Gifts and Rites.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12939-clive-coursor","name":"Clive Coursor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T04:36:39-08:00","id":1558315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clive Coursor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558280-mage-build-guys-i-m-a-fox?p=1558314#post1558314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get a hold of the old Werewolf Players guide I think they had Ware-Foxes in them and I think they had a Bread Book and showed up in the Year of the East books<br /> <br /> Perhaps you are a kitsune Kinfolk and instead of going through the Change you Awakened get a &quot;Warewolf Companion&quot; only 3 Freebie Points or if you don't want a connection to the actual kitsune take a few levels in Past Lives and Throwback to a past life that was a kitsune and take some magical prohibitions that line up with the kitsune. or mix and match from all of the above.<br /> <br /> try to model your Rotes after the kitsune Bread Gifts and Rites.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>If I understand correctly, the Kitsune can only reproduce in Asia. Those who are born outside the region will not undergo the First Change.<br /> <br /> Also, when they are born, at least one of their parents will always die at the same time.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> That being said, both the Dreamspeakers and the Akashic Brotherhood could make for appropriate Traditions to follow.<br /> <br /> Dreamspeakers, because of the Kitsune's connection to Gaia and the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Akashic Brotherhood, because of the eastern Asian culture and traditions.<br /> <br /> -----------------------<br /> <br /> Even if the mage in question is not an actual Kitsune, there's no reason to believe that it would be impossible for them to make that happen. The Bastet were created by a mage, while Samuel Haight learned about the <b>Ritual of Sacred Rebirth</b> from the Verbena. Then you have Pentex's attempts at creating the Mockery Breeds, which were met with mixed results.<br /> <br /> So the potential for a magically induced transformation exists, they just need to figure out how to work it into their spell casting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T08:23:19-08:00","id":1558316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clive Coursor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1558280-mage-build-guys-i-m-a-fox?p=1558314#post1558314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">get a hold of the old Werewolf Players guide I think they had Ware-Foxes in them and I think they had a Bread Book and showed up in the Year of the East books<br /> <br /> Perhaps you are a kitsune Kinfolk and instead of going through the Change 