quot;romantic&quot; somehow). Disparate tend to be more rigid with their cultural background and practices than the Traditions.<br /> <br /> Closest non-Marauder that come to mind:<br /> <br /> The Verbena often believe their magick comes from magical bloodlines. I could see some Verbena-like families believing their ancestor was a fox. So you have reasons to believe you could be a fox.<br /> <br /> Some weird dreamspeakers that were taught by spirits also come to mind - such a character could have been led to believe his soul it's that of a kitsune (something interesting about this is that, if his Avatar manifest that way, the mage's own spiritual body could resemble a kitsune while in the Umbra).<br /> <br /> Of course, you could be an Orphan and just ally with whomever. <hr /> It isn't normal for Mages to just get a random &quot;delusion&quot; imposed on them when they Awaken (unless they awake to Marauderdoom). They, if anything, see reality more clearly than ever - then delude themselves because everyone has to understand what they see under some parameter or pre-conception, and a mage's power adjusts to better fit those parametters.<br /> <br /> A mage could believe he's a Kitsune because his Avatar it's one and they saw themselves reflected as such on Dreams. Or because of ancient legends on his locale talking about fox-people living among humans that have the powers you manifested at a time of peril - &quot;you're a fox, Harry&quot;. Maybe they were a therian that already believed to be a fox, so now that he's magick I guess he has to be a <i>magical</i> fox ... etc ... If I were the ST, I would ask why you suddenly became to believe you're a fox. Unless the character it's being manipulated by some entity that wants them to believe that uncritically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you are right with that, so I'll comment it to my PM and see what we can do. I really like this idea, thank you for your input &lt;3<br /> <br /> And yes! His avatar does resembles as a kitsune when hi awakaned (in a fire) and before that, in dreams or sometimes it felt like something he saw out of the corner of his eye, sometimes even like seeing tails or that his eyes resembled those of a fox in the mirror for a sec","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28959-damedrac","user":"Damedrac","date":". 02-14-2026, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28959-damedrac","name":"Damedrac","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-14T10:29:46-08:00","id":1558320,"title":"","content":"The werefoxes are in the <b>Hengeyokai </b>book. Most of the book is Asian Shifters and the were foxes are in the back.<br /> <br /> Although parents dying when a Kitsune is born is common, there are exceptions, you roll and your Kitsume might not have had either parent die.<br /> <br /> That said, death of a non kitsume parent is so common that kitsume chose to seduce Mages to kill them.<br /> <br /> A Mage who thinks that they are a kitsume might be related to Kitsume or being targeted by one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-18T11:27:18-08:00","id":1558375,"title":"","content":"Spheres-wise, what are you trying to do? Right now it sounds like a lot of enhanced range trickery and a little bit of small teleportation (Correspondence 2) with dramatically enhanced senses either physical (Forces), emotional (Mind), or spiritual (Spirit). Forces senses are likely the most versatile, but Mind the most useful in any social situation, and Spirit giving aura sensing and the ability to see across the gauntlet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T03:15:12-08:00","id":1558378,"title":"","content":"Id be tempted to play it straight and not have them as fera linked.<br /> <br /> Could be fun idea either. If you do decide they're kinfolk, dont bother with gifts they're a xp dead end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T08:52:54-08:00","id":1558380,"title":"","content":"A 2/1 Sphere split is really hard to well... do anything much with. I would offer up Entropy as a good fit for a character that plays around with luck or tricks; Sense Weakness could even have a predatory aspect to it if desired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-02-19T10:16:43-08:00","id":1558382,"title":"","content":"For trickster themes:<br /> <br /> Correspondence 2 offers powerful information gathering through extended range of both senses and sensory spells. The small object teleportation also allows for impressive sleight of hand because that's essentially what it is, manipulation of objects at sensory range rather than end of your arm range.<br /> <br /> Entropy 2 offers impressive ability to manipulate events indirectly.<br /> <br /> Forces 2 can be used for some really good instantaneous action boosts, but more importantly for a trickster can create illusions of sight, sound, and touch. There are range limitations and at least some indication that interactive illusions require (or are at least much easier) with Body of Light from Prime 2.<br /> <br /> Life 2 allows for enough shapechanging to look like other people and change identifying qualities like fingerprints or blood type.<br /> <br /> The others, even Mind 2, are potentially useful to a trickster, but mostly in the same way they are useful to anyone. <br /> <br /> As for the level 1 sphere, it is mostly sensory but some of the interesting options are:<br /> <br /> Entropy 1 can sense weak points and lies.<br /> <br /> Mind 1 can sense emotions and the presence of other minds, as well as read lingering emotions. So its quite useful for information gathering for a social trickster.<br /> <br /> Spirit 1 can read auras.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-23T06:58:23-07:00","id":1562081,"title":"","content":"I'm curious to know how this ended up in play by this point, though I also think the starting Spheres are too punishing for a Mage game, unless that's not just this one character.<br /> <br /> But I really think this character would be Orphan, period, unless infiltrating a faction.<br /> <br /> The belief in not being a Mage at all is really at odds with most factions on principle. Why would the character join or be accepted if they don't follow a Paradigm?<br /> <br /> And if they do... Being a fox is the least relevant part. All kinds of reasons could justify this Mage in any faction at all, even the Union. Only the Crafts could impose enough restriction on this regard as they regularly demand more than just buy in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}